                        



Item #:  SCP-5161

Object Class:  Safe Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5161 instances are to be contained in a standard humanoid containment cell. Containment cell is to be decorated as an ordinary living room, suitable for a child. SCP-5161 instances do not require sustenance as far as is currently known. It is advised to spray them once a week with water, to keep them clean and docile.

Containment cell is to be monitored at all times by personnel with level two (2) or higher clearance. Camera use is installed. Two armed guards are to be stationed outside of the containment cell. SCP-5161 instances require coloring materials such as pencils and papers to keep content. It is obligated to check once a week if current materials do suffice, if not new ones must be delivered as soon as possible.

Description:  SCP-5161-A  is a full-grown broccoli (Brassica oleracea var. Italica) SCP-5161-A appears to be sapient and exhibits intelligence and common knowledge consistent with that of a human child aged 4 (four). Through testing, composition of the subject revealed no unusual qualities that make it discernible from a non-sapient broccoli. Instance shows signs of higher brain functions and is considered to be sapient. It is currently unknown how SCP-5161-A perceives the world, since no humanlike senses are to be found. Investigations are still ongoing.

SCP-5161-A was discovered and brought into containment by Agent ████ █████ on ██/██/198█, who was at the time embedded as an undercover agent in █████, The Netherlands.

SCP-5161-A is able to communicate through anomalous means. Current studies show SCP-5161-A is able to move items through telekinetic manner. Strength level shown in telekinetic episodes is inconsistent, though instance is always able to write and draw.

Drawings and letters are consistent with drawings of a human child aged 4 (four). All drawings are crude and written words are written poorly, as to be expected from a small child. Written words appear to be of Dutch origin, translations are required.

Since retrieval in 198█ no changes have been found within SCP-5161-A. Subject does not seem to age biologically or mentally. Subject has however anomalous powers over other pieces of fruit and vegetables. Testing has shown nearby fruits and vegetables are safe for human consumption for longer extended periods of time. No nearby fruits and vegetables are to be held close to the containment cell. Non-anomalous fruits and vegetables seem to distress subject. Subject is believed to be distressed since normal food does not seem to communicate with SCP-5161 instances. Subject believes to be ignored and said action will trigger an distress event. Distress event seems to enlarge telekinetic strength level and give the subject more power to hold heavier objects. SCP-5161 instances are able to move furniture and tremble the containment cell during times of distress.

SCP-5161 instances are believed to be safe since containment is without challenge. Instances are docile in their containment cell. Distress events may harm foundation personnel, though testing has shown SCP-5161 does not wish to willfully harm humans. Since addendum SCP-5161-C object class has been promoted to Euclid. Armed guards are to be stationed outside of perimeter. No food is to be allowed near containment cell so no distress events will occur.

Personnel bringing any foods close enough to SCP-5161 instances are to be demoted to D-Class. No events must be triggered for as long as possible. D-Class personnel may be terminated upon violating these rules.

SCP-5161-B  is a full grown Cauliflower (Brassica oleracea var. botrytis) and appears to have the same qualities as SCP-5161-A. SCP-5161 instances are to be kept in the same containment cell, instances seem to hold each other in high regard.

SCP-5161-B has been retrieved in 1994 in █████, Norway. Foundation agent ████ █████ has retrieved instance from a local supermarket. No breach of secrecy has occured and object has been safely retrieved at Site-██. Instances seem to have acknowledge some sort of family bond even though testing has shown instances do not seem to understand each other verbally. Anomalous means of communicating are expected.

SCP-5161-B appears to be sapient and exhibits intelligence and common knowledge consistent with that of a human child aged 6 (six). Drawings and letters are present, though these are written in Norwegian. SCP-5161 instances seem to have a language barrier between each other, ongoing studies have to show how these instances communicate with this barrier. Ongoing anomalous means are currently suspected.

SCP-5161-C  is a full grown parsnip (Pastinaca sativa) and has been in foundation custody since 201█. Subject has been retrieved from Site-██’s cafeteria. An unknown foundation personnel has brought subject into Site-██. During lunchbreak SCP-5161-C got severely distressed resulting in SCP-5161-C event (see addendum SCP-5161-C)

Unknown foundation personnel brought SCP-5161-C from home to consume during lunchbreak. Current studies have shown to trigger severe distress from subject when in view of a sharp object, such as a knife. It is currently not known how SCP-5161-C sees the world around it, since no senses have been shown during testing.

Origins of SCP-5161-C are not known, because the foundation personnel that brought it into the facility has died during SCP-5161-C event and the containment breach that occurred during this episode. Subject appears to be sapient and exhibits intelligence and common knowledge consistent with that of a human child aged 2 (two). Testing has shown no unusual qualities to make it discernible from a non-sapient parsnip.

Drawings are produced by SCP-5161-C but lack severely in quality as expected of a small child. Current drawings offer no conclusion to the origin of subject, language or other significant details.

During the last years all three instances of SCP-5161 seem to have bonded together. It is currently unknown if all instances spark from the same origin, though this does seem to be unlikely since subjects were found in different countries and different years.

By unknown anomalous means (suspected telepathy) are instances ‘able to communicate’ with each other. It is unknown what instances tell each other, if they even speak. It is not known how these instances communicate since they do not appear to speak each other languages.

Addendum SCP-5161-C 

An unknown foundation personnel brought SCP-5161-C into containment, unknowingly, on 16-9-201█. During lunchbreak subject was experiencing increasing levels of trauma causing distress. Current theory is the subject startled in view of the knife, testing afterwards seems to cause the same effect but less dramatic when close to other SCP-5161 instances.

Current SCP-5161 instances were known to have access to anomalous means, most notably telekinesis. The same effect is present in SCP-5161-C but far stronger especially observed during this event. Priorly unknown to the foundation the subject also able to put out a regional electro magnetic pulse blast (EMP) resulting in the containment breach of six (6) other SCP’s. This effect cost the lives of ██ foundation personnel while injuring ██ more.

Camera’s and surveillance footage were unable to be reviewed as any live cameras were destroyed in the process of the episode. Due to unavailable footage it is currently not known who brought SCP-5161-C into Site-██. Investigations to retain other footage through interviews is still ongoing.

Nearby MTF units were able to re-contain the other assets within approximately three (3) hours. During these hours another ██ foundation personnel were lost; making in total ██ lost foundation personnel while another ██ were injured during the process.

Because of this event SCP-5161 instances have to be kept in a docile state and content in their containment cell. Object class has been promoted to Euclid by the approval of Dr. █████ and 05-█.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    

                    
                    
                        
